{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After this opened Job his mouth, and cursed his day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Job answered and said:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the day perish wherein I was born,\nAnd the night which said, There is a man-child conceived.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let that day be darkness;\nLet not God from above seek for it,\nNeither let the light shine upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let darkness and the shadow of death claim it for their own;\nLet a cloud dwell upon it;\nLet all that maketh black the day terrify it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for that night, let thick darkness seize upon it:\nLet it not rejoice among the days of the year;\nLet it not come into the number of the months.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, let that night be barren;\nLet no joyful voice come therein.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them curse it that curse the day,\nWho are ready to rouse up leviathan.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the stars of the twilight thereof be dark:\nLet it look for light, but have none;\nNeither let it behold the eyelids of the morning:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because it shut not up the doors of my ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mother’s",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " womb,\nNor hid trouble from mine eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why died I not from the womb?\nWhy did I not give up the ghost when my mother bare me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why did the knees receive me?\nOr why the breasts, that I should suck?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For now should I have lain down and been quiet;\nI should have slept; then had I been at rest,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With kings and counsellors of the earth,\nWho built up waste places for themselves;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or with princes that had gold,\nWho filled their houses with silver:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or as a hidden untimely birth I had not been,\nAs infants that never saw light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There the wicked cease from troubling;\nAnd there the weary are at rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There the prisoners are at ease together;\nThey hear not the voice of the taskmaster.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The small and the great are there:\nAnd the servant is free from his master.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore is light given to him that is in misery,\nAnd life unto the bitter in soul;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who long for death, but it cometh not,\nAnd dig for it more than for hid treasures;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who rejoice exceedingly,\nAnd are glad, when they can find the grave?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why is light given",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to a man whose way is hid,\nAnd whom God hath hedged in?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For my sighing cometh before I eat,\nAnd my groanings are poured out like water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the thing which I fear cometh upon me,\nAnd that which I am afraid of cometh unto me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.3.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am not at ease, neither am I quiet, neither have I rest;\nBut trouble cometh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
